<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $123.9 mln Feb 25.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $123.9 mln Feb 25.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $123.9 million deficit on Feb 25 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON FEBRUARY 25</p>
<p>Exports: $159 million</p>
<p>Imports: $230.4 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $224.5 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $277 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $123.9 million</p>
<p>FEBRUARY DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.711 million</p>
<p>Imports: $2.733 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $3.999 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $2.978 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $999 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248-5418</p>
</text>
